---

1. Introduction

1.1 Purpose

This Software Requirements Specification defines the functional and non-functional requirements of AI-TRAVELMATE, an intelligent travel planning and recommendation system.

The document describes the system's purpose, scope, architecture, interfaces, data requirements, user interactions, constraints, and testing criteria.

It is intended for project developers, testers, evaluators, and other stakeholders involved in the design, implementation, and validation of the application.

1.2 Project Scope

AI-TRAVELMATE is a web application that helps users discover destinations, receive personalized travel recommendations, obtain weather information, calculate routes, and generate travel itineraries.

The application will combine external data sources with a recommendation engine, a traffic prediction component where suitable data is available, and an AI assistant that explains the resulting recommendations.

The initial release will focus on a limited, testable set of features rather than a complete commercial travel-booking platform.

The system will not claim to provide live traffic information unless it is connected to a reliable and permitted live traffic data source.

1.3 Intended Audience

This document is intended for:

- Frontend developers.
- Backend developers.
- Machine learning developers.
- Database designers.
- Software testers.
- Academic project supervisors.
- Project evaluators and stakeholders.

