4. Functional Requirements

4.1 Destination Search

FR-01: The system shall allow users to enter a destination name or location.

FR-02: The system shall return relevant destination or point-of-interest results when supported data is available.

FR-03: The system shall allow users to filter results by supported categories.

FR-04: The system shall display available destination information, including name, category, coordinates, and other relevant metadata.

FR-05: The system shall inform users when a search produces no results.

4.2 Travel Preferences

FR-06: The system shall allow users to enter a starting location.

FR-07: The system shall allow users to specify travel interests.

FR-08: The system shall allow users to specify an approximate budget.

FR-09: The system shall allow users to specify trip duration or travel dates.

FR-10: The system shall validate required inputs before processing a recommendation request.

FR-11: The system shall allow users to revise their preferences and request updated recommendations.

4.3 Personalized Recommendations

FR-12: The system shall calculate recommendation scores for candidate destinations.

FR-13: The system shall rank destinations according to the selected preferences and available information.

FR-14: The recommendation algorithm shall use configurable weights for preference match, budget suitability, travel-time suitability, and weather suitability.

FR-15: The system shall explain the primary reasons for a recommendation.

FR-16: The system shall handle missing destination information without silently treating unknown values as confirmed negative values.

FR-17: The system shall display a suitable message when insufficient information is available to generate meaningful recommendations.

4.4 Weather Information

FR-18: The system shall retrieve weather information for a selected destination when supported by the chosen weather service.

FR-19: The system shall display available weather variables such as temperature and precipitation information.

FR-20: The system shall display forecast dates or timestamps when available.

FR-21: The system shall use available weather information to influence relevant outdoor-activity recommendations.

FR-22: The system shall display an appropriate message when weather data is unavailable or cannot be retrieved.

FR-23: The system shall not present expired or unavailable weather data as verified current information.

4.5 Route Planning

FR-24: The system shall allow users to select a starting point and destination.

FR-25: The system shall request route calculations from the configured routing service.

FR-26: The system shall display the calculated route on a map when route geometry is available.

FR-27: The system shall display estimated distance and journey duration when returned by the routing service.

FR-28: The system shall support the creation of an itinerary containing multiple destinations.

FR-29: The system shall handle unavailable routes and invalid coordinates gracefully.

FR-30: The system shall distinguish ordinary route-duration estimates from traffic-adjusted travel times.

4.6 Traffic Prediction

FR-31: The system shall support a traffic prediction component when a suitable model and compatible input data are available.

FR-32: The prediction component shall accept the features required by its trained model.

FR-33: The system shall produce a predicted traffic value or category according to the model's defined output.

FR-34: The system shall identify predicted traffic results as predictions.

FR-35: The system shall identify live traffic results as live only when supported by a reliable current traffic data source.

FR-36: The system shall not label historical averages, simulated data, or model predictions as live observations.

FR-37: The system shall record the data source and relevant timestamp for traffic observations when such information is available.

FR-38: The system shall provide an appropriate fallback message when the required traffic input data is unavailable.

FR-39: The model shall be evaluated against a suitable baseline before its performance is described as improved or accurate.

FR-40: Traffic prediction results shall not be represented as guaranteed journey times.

4.7 AI Travel Assistant

FR-41: The system shall accept travel-related user questions through a supported interface.

FR-42: The assistant shall generate explanations based on available destination, route, weather, and recommendation data.

FR-43: The assistant shall use the selected language model or another configured generation method.

FR-44: The assistant shall not invent unavailable live traffic conditions, weather observations, destination details, or service responses.

FR-45: The assistant shall communicate uncertainty or data limitations when relevant.

FR-46: The system shall handle AI model errors and unavailable model services gracefully.

4.8 Itinerary Generation

FR-47: The system shall generate a proposed itinerary from selected destinations and user preferences.

FR-48: The itinerary shall consider available route distances and estimated journey durations.

FR-49: The itinerary shall consider weather information when relevant and available.

FR-50: The system shall allow users to add or remove destinations from a proposed itinerary.

FR-51: The system shall allow users to review and modify the proposed order of destinations.

FR-52: The system shall indicate when opening hours or other planning information has not been verified.

4.9 Saved Trips

FR-53: If persistence functionality is enabled, the system shall allow users to save an itinerary.

FR-54: If account functionality is enabled, the system shall associate saved trips with the appropriate authenticated user.

FR-55: The system shall allow authorized users to retrieve and update their saved itineraries.

FR-56: The system shall prevent one authenticated user from accessing another user's private saved trips.

Account and saved-trip functionality may be deferred if it is not required for the initial demonstration.

4.10 Error Handling

FR-57: The system shall validate user input.

FR-58: The system shall handle external API failures without crashing the entire application.

FR-59: The system shall return understandable error messages for failed requests.

FR-60: The system shall log relevant backend errors without exposing sensitive information.

FR-61: The system shall distinguish unavailable data from valid empty results.

