10. Security and Privacy Requirements

The system shall:

- Store credentials securely.
- Avoid exposing private API keys in frontend code.
- Validate user input on the backend.
- Use secure database access practices.
- Apply authorization checks if user accounts are implemented.
- Restrict access to private saved itineraries.
- Avoid logging passwords, API keys, and unnecessary personal data.
- Request permission before accessing device location.
- Document the handling of stored user information.

Public deployment must include a review of applicable privacy, security, and external-service requirements.

