11. Error Handling and Recovery

11.1 Network Failure

The application shall show a clear message when an external service cannot be reached.

11.2 Rate Limit Exceeded

The application shall respect provider rate limits and may retry after an appropriate delay where permitted.

11.3 Invalid User Input

The system shall reject invalid coordinates, malformed requests, or unsupported parameters with an understandable message.

11.4 Missing Data

The system shall identify missing information instead of fabricating values.

11.5 Traffic Model Failure

The system shall indicate that a prediction is unavailable if the model fails or required input features are missing.

11.6 AI Model Failure

The application shall communicate when the AI assistant is unavailable and retain access to other application features where possible.

11.7 Database Failure

The application shall return a suitable error response when persistence operations cannot be completed. It shall not report a save operation as successful if the database write fails.

