12. Testing Requirements

12.1 Unit Testing

Test individual components, including:

- Input validation.
- Recommendation scoring.
- Weather-response processing.
- Route-response processing.
- Traffic feature preparation.
- Traffic prediction output handling.
- Itinerary ordering.

12.2 Integration Testing

Test:

- Frontend-to-backend communication.
- Backend-to-weather-service communication.
- Backend-to-routing-service communication.
- Destination data retrieval.
- Database persistence where implemented.
- AI model integration.
- Traffic prediction integration.

12.3 Functional Testing

Verify that users can search destinations, enter preferences, obtain recommendations, review route and weather information, and generate itineraries.

12.4 Performance Testing

Measure response time and resource usage under representative test conditions.

12.5 Security Testing

Test input validation, access control where implemented, credential handling, and protection of private saved data.

12.6 Machine Learning Evaluation

For traffic prediction:

- Use a time-based train/test split.
- Compare predictions against a simple baseline.
- Measure MAE and RMSE for numerical predictions.
- Evaluate classification metrics if congestion categories are predicted.
- Avoid data leakage between training and testing.
- Document the geographic coverage and limitations of the dataset.

12.7 Usability Testing

Ask representative users to complete basic travel-planning tasks and identify usability issues.

