13. Acceptance Criteria

The system shall be accepted for the initial MVP demonstration when:

1. Destination search returns relevant results when supported data is available.
2. Users can submit travel preferences.
3. The recommendation engine produces ranked destinations.
4. Available weather information is displayed with appropriate context.
5. Route calculations display distance and estimated duration when returned by the service.
6. Users can generate and modify a proposed itinerary.
7. The AI assistant explains recommendations using available application data.
8. Traffic predictions are labeled accurately and are not misrepresented as live observations.
9. Missing data and external service failures are handled gracefully.
10. The application can be installed and run using the supplied setup instructions.
11. The main functional and integration tests pass.
12. Data-source attribution and relevant usage requirements are documented.

If live traffic data is not available, the MVP may still be demonstrated using clearly labeled traffic predictions or historical estimates, provided the traffic limitations are explained.

