15. Limitations

The initial system has the following limitations:

- Weather accuracy depends on the selected weather provider and forecast horizon.
- Destination coverage depends on the completeness of the available geographical data.
- Route estimates depend on the selected routing engine and its underlying road data.
- Basic open routing services do not inherently provide real-time traffic congestion.
- Traffic prediction depends on representative historical and current input data.
- A model trained on a foreign city cannot automatically be assumed to predict Indian city traffic accurately.
- AI-generated explanations may require validation and careful grounding.
- Public free services may enforce rate limits or change availability.
- Recommendation quality depends on the reliability of destination metadata and the suitability of scoring weights.

These limitations shall be considered during evaluation and documented in the final project report.

